  "question": "Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a package for AdonisJS that provides role-based permissions integrated with Adonis Auth. This system manages user roles and permissions, facilitating secure access control within applications built on AdonisJS.\n\nObjectives\n\nThe primary objective is to implement a robust access control layer allowing administrators to assign roles and permissions to users efficiently. This will ensure that users have appropriate access levels tailored to their roles within the application.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Administrators: Manage roles and permissions, assign roles to users.\n- Developers: Integrate the package into AdonisJS projects.\n- End-Users: Perform actions based on assigned roles and permissions.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Role Management: \n   - Create, read, update, and delete roles.\n   - Associate roles with specific permissions.\n\n2. Permission Management: \n   - Create, read, update, and delete permissions.\n   - Associate permissions with roles and users.\n\n3. User Role Assignment: \n   - Assign and remove roles from users.\n   - Modify user roles as needed.\n\n4. Access Control:\n   - Ensure users access resources based on assigned roles and permissions.\n   - Integrate with Adonis Auth for authentication management.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n1. Performance: \n   - Efficiently support concurrent access for enterprise-level applications.\n   \n2. Security: \n   - Protect sensitive data and ensure secure operation aligned with Adonis Auth.\n   \n3. Scalability: \n   - Easily extendable to accommodate additional roles and permissions as needed.\n\n4. Usability: \n   - Intuitive interface for administrators to manage roles and permissions effectively.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0082\nCREATE TABLE `roles` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `slug` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `roles_slug_unique` (`slug`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `permissions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `slug` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `permissions_slug_unique` (`slug`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `users_email_unique` (`email`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `role_permissions` (\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `permission_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`role_id`,`permission_id`),\n  KEY `role_permissions_permission_id_index` (`permission_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `role_permissions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `roles` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `role_permissions_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`permission_id`) REFERENCES `permissions` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_roles` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`,`role_id`),\n  KEY `user_roles_role_id_index` (`role_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_roles_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_roles_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `roles` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_permissions` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `permission_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`,`permission_id`),\n  KEY `user_permissions_permission_id_index` (`permission_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_permissions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_permissions_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`permission_id`) REFERENCES `permissions` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
